  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday night through next Saturday)\nIssued at 1058 PM CDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nHigh pressure will build once again across northern Mexico on Monday \nwhile another low comes ashore across California.  This will \nincrease monsoon moisture from late Monday peaking Wednesday \nfocusing a bit to our west, thence moving closer into the late week. \n This, in turn, will yield above average precipitation (storms) \nactivity for the week.  If you're looking for sunny skies across \nWest Texas, this isn't the week. The risk of the stronger downburst \ndays looks to diminish as the week progresses as LCLs sharply lower \nwith increased RH given the lower high temperatures.  In fact, we \nhave a number of days where highs may stick to the 70s across \nportions of our area.  Granted, the guidance has been a bit \noverzealous on cooling temperatures in the extended this fall, but \neventually, fall will take hold.",
